# Browser
# Cuombajj Witches in a game of three: its "any target of an opponent's choice" has two opponents to leave it to, so
# Bot1's page is first asked which one chooses, and says what that player will do - choose targets for the ability, not
# "choose targets" as a sentence of its own (CR 115.1, 608.2d). Bot1 picks Bot2, who then chooses Bot3 for the second target.
[Bot1 Deck]
Cuombajj Witches
Mox Jet
Gleemox
Swamp x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20
[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Gleemox.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Gleemox.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Cuombajj Witches.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cuombajj Witches.Activate
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Cuombajj Witches: choose an opponent
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = The player you choose chooses targets for the ability of Cuombajj Witches
Bot1.ChoosePlayer(Bot2)
Bot2.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot3.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Cuombajj Witches.Tapped = true
